e  supporting spider-man and then even got  the email address from eige and  contacted him afterwards however the  topic was not about spider-man but about  the opportunity to thank him for the  last five years Bob Iger also seemed to  have responded quickly and called  Holland shortly afterwards as Holland  tells it at an inconvenient time for him  since Holland had already had three  beers and was not quite as sober anymore  in the following telephone conversation  even cried and convinced Agra so far  that he was said to have said that there  was a world in the negotiations with  Sony where you could do that the rest is  history because shortly afterwards the  turnaround happened and the deal was  extended to what extent Tom Hollands  actually contributed to this is of  course questionable but it could be that  he was the tip of the iceberg for  spider-man's future in the MCU it has  been known for some time that the third  part of the conjuring series won't be a  pure haunted house horror movie instead  the two ghost Honda's ed and Lorraine  Warren will be confronted with a whole  new kind of evil as the title of the  film which was revealed this week  suggests because it bears the name the  conjuring the devil made me do it  instead of a ghost house this time the  warrants will take care of a little boy  soul the story which will push the  self-proclaimed demonologist to their  limits is again based on true events and  deals with the first case in the history  of American justice in which a murder  suspect wants to claim demon possession  as a defense ground concluding words are  given by a leading actor Patrick Wilson  who told in an interview with The  Hollywood Reporter that the movie still  has the same framework it's still aired  in Lorraine again they will push their  characters to places they haven't gone  yet but the movie will be a really nice  addition because it's definitely a  completely different monster the  conjuring the devil made me do it will  be released on September 11th 2020 in  u.s. cinemas at the moment director  George Miller is still working on his  new movie 3,000 years of longing but the  next project after that is already fixed  namely Mad Max in the past there were  some financial problems with this  project so the fifth offshoot of the  series was often postponed  however this now seems to belong to the  Past because as the director announced  there was finally an agreement Miller  explains that he's already in the middle  of preparation that the story of Mad Max  isn't finished yet  and that another Mad Max part will  surely follow the directors already  stages the letter several times in the  past  allegedly even the script for the sequel  is already finished however we have to  wait quite some time until the shooting  starts because first of all the shooting  for our three  colleges of longing is scheduled to  start in March next year  [Music]

